From: Davi <davilimacarv2536@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 13 Sep 2026 22:38:42 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 2/6] embedder memory budget

Lets an embedder that forks give each child its own memory budget after
the fork, in the two places where the engine weighs its work against
memory. Both hooks are process-local, because the figures the engine
uses by default are computed once, before the fork, and every child
inherits them.

`setColloGCMaxHeapSizeOverride` replaces `Options::gcMaxHeapSize` in
the collection trigger through `JSC::effectiveGCMaxHeapSize`. With
`USE(BUN_JSC_ADDITIONS)`, `Heap::collectIfNecessaryOrDefer` requests a
collection as soon as the bytes allocated since the last one pass it,
and the heap's own trigger still runs below it. The option itself
cannot carry a child's value: JSC's options live in the configuration
pages that `VM` creation freezes read-only, so they are fixed before
the first fork.

`setColloMemoryStatusOverride` makes `WTF::memoryStatus` measure the
process against the embedder's budget. `Heap::overCriticalMemoryThreshold`
compares that status with `criticalGCMemoryThreshold` to decide full
collections, synchronous sweeps and a smaller collection budget. On
Linux the status is the resident size read from a `/proc/self/statm`
descriptor that the first call opens and keeps, over `availableMemory()`,
which the first call computes and keeps. A child forked after those
calls inherits the parent's limit and a descriptor number it may have
closed; a sandboxed child cannot reopen statm, and the number may by
then name another file, which the engine then parses as statm. With the
override, the footprint is the byte count in a cgroup v2
`memory.current` descriptor the embedder opened, and the share in use
is that footprint over the limit it passed, so critical mode engages at
`criticalGCMemoryThreshold` of the child's own budget. A lock held
across the read lets `clearColloMemoryStatusOverride` guarantee that no
thread reads the descriptor after it returns. `availableMemory()` and
the heap sizing derived from it keep their inherited values.
